# public/sitemap.xml is a generated artifact: scripts/generate-sitemap.mjs always
# writes LF. On Windows with core.autocrlf=true, checkout rewrote it to CRLF, so
# every `npm run build` re-flagged the file as modified in `git status` even
# though the content was byte-identical after normalisation. Pinning this one
# generated file to LF makes the checked-out bytes match what the generator
# writes, which keeps the build side-effect-free locally and preserves the
# "no tracked file was modified by the build" check in .github/workflows/build.yml.
#
# Deliberately scoped to this single path. Repository-wide line-ending behaviour
# is intentionally left untouched.
public/sitemap.xml text eol=lf
